1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Welcome to this training on the Demo Retail greeting standard. In the next few minutes you will learn exactly what great first contact with a customer looks like on our shop floor.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Every customer who enters your section should be acknowledged within ten seconds. That does not always mean stopping what you are doing. A smile, eye contact, or a simple nod tells the customer: I have seen you, and I am here.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:41,000
When you are free, greet the customer warmly. Say: welcome, how can I help you today? Keep your body language open. Face the customer, keep your hands visible, and never greet from behind a shelf or with your back turned.

4
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:58,000
If you are busy with another customer, do not ignore the person waiting. Make brief eye contact and say: I will be with you in a moment. Most customers are happy to wait once they know they have been noticed.

5
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Listening comes before answering. Let the customer finish their question completely before you respond. If you are not sure what they need, ask one clarifying question. For example: are you looking for the fresh section or the packaged one?

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:33,000
If you cannot help, never just point. Walk the customer to the right aisle or to a colleague who can help. We call this the walk, not point rule. It takes thirty seconds and it is the single behaviour customers remember most.

7
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Now let us talk about difficult moments. When a customer is upset, use the LAST method. Listen without interrupting. Apologize sincerely. Solve what you can on the spot. Thank them for telling us. Raise your team leader early if the situation grows beyond you.

8
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Remember: staying calm is professional strength. Lower your voice when a customer raises theirs. Never argue about who is right. Your goal is that the customer leaves feeling respected, even when the answer is no.

9
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:25,000
To summarise: acknowledge within ten seconds. Greet warmly with open body language. Listen fully before answering. Walk, do not point. And use the LAST method when things get difficult. That is the Demo Retail service standard.
